{"id":"transamerica-trail","title":"TransAmerica Bike Trail","who":"Classic touring route (Bikecentennial, 1976)","when":"Since 1976","vehicle":"Touring or road bike","kind":"bike","color":"#be123c","summary":"About 6,800 km coast to coast on quiet roads, from the Pacific in Oregon to the Atlantic in Virginia, through the Cascades, Yellowstone, the Rockies, the plains, the Ozarks and Appalachia. Created for America's bicentennial, when thousands rode it.","sources":[{"label":"Wikipedia: TransAmerica Trail (bicycle)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/TransAmerica_Trail_(bicycle)"}],"approximate":"Towns on the route; the line between them is approximate (use the official maps to ride it).","km":6167,"bbox":[-123.8318,36.5702,-76.5079,46.8776],"stops":[{"name":"Astoria","place":"Astoria, Oregon","at":[46.1882,-123.832],"text":"Dip your wheel in the Pacific at the mouth of the Columbia River.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Astoria_Oregon.jpg/500px-Astoria_Oregon.jpg","page":"Astoria, Oregon","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Astoria_Oregon.jpg","credit":"BeachcombersNW","license":"CC BY 2.0"}},{"name":"McKenzie Pass","place":"Sisters, Oregon","at":[44.2909,-121.5493],"text":"Over the Cascades through old lava fields.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/McKenziePassOR242.png/500px-McKenziePassOR242.png","page":"McKenzie Pass","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:McKenziePassOR242.png","credit":"David Hunter from Nashville, TN, USA","license":"CC BY 2.0"}},{"name":"Baker City","place":"Baker City, Oregon","at":[44.7749,-117.8344],"text":"Eastern Oregon's dry hills.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Bakermainstreet.jpg/500px-Bakermainstreet.jpg","page":"Baker City, Oregon","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bakermainstreet.jpg","credit":"Finetooth","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0"}},{"name":"Missoula","place":"Missoula, Montana","at":[46.8701,-113.9953],"text":"Home of Adventure Cycling, where riders stop for a photo.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Missoula%2C_Montana.jpg/500px-Missoula%2C_Montana.jpg","page":"Missoula, Montana","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Missoula%2C_Montana.jpg","credit":"Quintin Soloviev","license":"CC BY 4.0"}},{"name":"Yellowstone","place":"West Yellowstone, Montana","at":[44.6632,-111.1012],"text":"Geysers and bison in Yellowstone.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/60/Grand_Canyon_of_the_Yellowstone_Lower_Falls_%2895819p%29.jpg/500px-Grand_Canyon_of_the_Yellowstone_Lower_Falls_%2895819p%29.jpg","page":"Yellowstone National Park","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Grand_Canyon_of_the_Yellowstone_Lower_Falls_%2895819p%29.jpg","credit":"Rhododendrites","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}},{"name":"Grand Tetons","place":"Jackson, Wyoming","at":[43.48,-110.7618],"text":"Under the Tetons.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/Barns_grand_tetons.jpg/500px-Barns_grand_tetons.jpg","page":"Grand Teton National Park","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Barns_grand_tetons.jpg","credit":"Jon Sullivan, PD Photo.","license":"Public domain"}},{"name":"Wyoming","place":"Rawlins, Wyoming","at":[41.7908,-107.2392],"text":"Big skies and long empty roads.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/DowntownRawlins.jpg/500px-DowntownRawlins.jpg","page":"Rawlins, Wyoming","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:DowntownRawlins.jpg","credit":"Vasiliymeshko","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}},{"name":"Hoosier Pass","place":"Breckenridge, Colorado","at":[39.4829,-106.0465],"text":"Hoosier Pass, the highest point of the route.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/HoosierPass.jpg/500px-HoosierPass.jpg","page":"Hoosier Pass","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:HoosierPass.jpg","credit":"Ken Gallager at English Wikipedia","license":"Public domain"}},{"name":"Pueblo","place":"Pueblo, Colorado","at":[38.264,-104.6142],"text":"Down onto the plains.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Pueblo%2C_Colorado.jpg/500px-Pueblo%2C_Colorado.jpg","page":"Pueblo, Colorado","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pueblo%2C_Colorado.jpg","credit":"Quintin Soloviev","license":"CC BY 4.0"}},{"name":"Kansas","place":"Newton, Kansas","at":[38.0469,-97.3447],"text":"Wind, wheat and very straight roads."},{"name":"The Ozarks","place":"Ash Grove, Missouri","at":[37.3153,-93.5852],"text":"Short, steep hills in the Missouri Ozarks.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3b/Commercial_Street_Historic_District%2C_Springfield%2C_Missouri.jpg/500px-Commercial_Street_Historic_District%2C_Springfield%2C_Missouri.jpg","page":"Ozarks","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Commercial_Street_Historic_District%2C_Springfield%2C_Missouri.jpg","credit":"Diedrichb","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}},{"name":"Illinois","place":"Carbondale, Illinois","at":[37.7275,-89.2167],"text":"Across the Mississippi.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/SIUC_Faner.jpg/500px-SIUC_Faner.jpg","page":"Carbondale, Illinois","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:SIUC_Faner.jpg","credit":"Bradley Furlow","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}},{"name":"Kentucky","place":"Berea, Kentucky","at":[37.5687,-84.2963],"text":"Rolling Kentucky farmland, and its famous chasing dogs.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Berea_Kentucky_City_Hall.jpg/500px-Berea_Kentucky_City_Hall.jpg","page":"Berea, Kentucky","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Berea_Kentucky_City_Hall.jpg","credit":"Dwight Burdette","license":"CC BY 3.0"}},{"name":"Appalachians","place":"Damascus, Virginia","at":[36.635,-81.7888],"t